  "scope": "All eight former legacy PointSpatialIndex constructor sites across seven readiness consumers: edge/chassis stitching, return path, power via arrays, differential via proximity/return, and mouse-bite drills. Additive Real::fixed_decimal presentation view required by native mouse-bite diagnostics. The full 39-property, 14-target and crate future-work goal remains open.",
  "contract": [
    "Retain borrowed native point coordinates through conservative enclosure candidate selection and checked squared-radius predicates. Required unresolved decisions and unavailable markers produce geometry-uncertainty under the shared STRICT/budget guard, including empty and warm paths.",
    "Existence accepts any certified alternative; otherwise unresolved candidates cannot become certified absence. Power vias require distinct native centers. Native negative radii do not become positive by squaring.",
    "Mouse-bite eligibility and minimum/maximum pitch use required checked comparisons. A certified too-close pair proves a finding; optional nearest-bad ordering may retain the first certified pair. Display uses an explicit fixed-decimal projection and never decides pitch.",
    "Real::fixed_decimal reuses the existing absolute-precision Computable Display formatter, avoiding the scientific leading-bit search for unresolved near-zero values. General alternate/scientific formatting and universal resource bounds remain open."
  ],
